s a nonexistent image tag (v3.2.0); new pods are stuck in ImagePullBackOff, leaving 1/3 replicas to serve all traffic. _(confidence 90%)_\n\n### Supporting evidence\n\n- `ev-s4-k8s-1` (k8s_event, kubernetes): Failed to pull image aiops/user-service:v3.2.0: manifest unknown (ImagePullBackOff), 2 pods [link](http://localhost:3000/d/k8s-workloads/k8s-workloads?var-deployment=user-service&from=1790266200000&to=1790268000000)\n- `ev-s4-k8s-2` (k8s_event, kubernetes): Deployment user-service revision 6 (v3.2.0) at 16:21Z; replicas 1/3 available\n- `ev-s4-code-1` (commit, git): Commit a91e7c3 'bump user-service to v3.2.0' references an unreleased tag\n- `ev-s4-alerts-1` (alert, alertmanager): DeploymentReplicasMismatch (warning) since 16:31Z: 1/3 replicas available [link](http://localhost:9093/#/alerts?filter=%7Balertname%3D%22DeploymentReplicasMismatch%22%7D)\n- `ev-s4-logs-1` (log, elasticsearch): 38 '503 no healthy upstream' from callers; queue depth warnings on the one ready replica [link](http://localhost:5601/app/discover#/?_g=(time:(from:'2026-09-24T16:10:00Z',to:'2026-09-24T16:40:00Z'))&_a=(index:'user-prod-*',query:(language:kuery,query:'FROM%20user-prod-*%20%7C%20STATS%20count%20BY%20pattern')))\n\n## Impact\n\n503 on login and checkout for part of the traffic since 16:23Z; user-service at 33% capacity.\n\n## Timeline (UTC)\n\n- 16:15:00 Commit bumps image to v3.2.0 (unreleased) _(code)_\n- 16:21:00 Rollout of revision 6 starts _(k8s)_\n- 16:21:30 ImagePullBackOff on new pods _(k8s)_\n- 16:23:40 Queue pressure and 503s from callers _(logs)_\n- 16:31:00 DeploymentReplicasMismatch fires _(alerts)_\n\n## Next steps\n\n1. Roll back user-service (kubectl rollout undo).\n2. Fix the image tag in git before redeploying.\n\n## Open questions\n\n- Why did CI allow a manifest to reference an unbuilt image?\n\n_Generated by AI Incident Agents (demo mode)._"}}},{"type":"investigation_finished","investigation_id":"inv-demo-s4","timestamp":"2026-09-24T16:40:29.400Z","seq":43,"a